[Music]  thank you  hi guys it's Quinn here if you enjoy my  videos consider hitting the like button  it's the only way the YouTube algorithm  really notices me  now today we're going to talk about the  ixians so in the Dune series The ixians  were the inhabitants of a fringe world  at the edge of the Empire called IX now  IX was the ninth planet in its solar  system and the world of IX unlike most  planets had escaped the harshest effects  of the butlerian Jihad so this means  they were much more okay with machine  technology and even some technology that  pushed the prescriptions of the  butlerian Jihad now if you're not  familiar with the butlerian Jihad then  I've done several videos on it which you  can find in my Dune playlist on my  channel essentially about 10 000 years  before the start of the Dune series  mankind relied on intelligent machines  for just about everything when the  butlerian Jihad happened all thinking  machines were banished from the Empire  and the line Thou shalt not make a  machine in the likeness of a human mind  was added to their orange Catholic Bible  which was a big religious text in the  Dune University so basically any  Computing technology was banned now the  thing about the ixians is it is not  extremely clear in what ways and at what  times they are actually defying the  butlerian Jihad but it is clear that  they are now when it comes to the danger  of ixian technology and the danger of  technology in general as it's presented  in the Dune Universe there are two ways  we are meant to think about this one way  is the danger of human dependency on  technology if we become too dependent on  technology then in a situation when we  don't have it Society might collapse the  other way we're meant to think about  this is the potential danger of the  exponential growth of that technology  itself now this is what leicho II feared  the most about the ixians and this is  one of the main things that he worked so  hard to undo and God Emperor it says do  not fear the ixians he's said he heard  his own voice as a fading whisper they  can make the machines but they can no  longer make arafel I know I was there  now we've talked about this line before  on this channel rfl refers to the cloud  darkness of holy judgment it's a  Biblical reference  essentially he's saying don't worry  about the ixians I have made it so that  they can never create the technology  that would destroy all of humanity now I  will say that the ixians will still  produce this technology these seeking  machines that siona Atreides herself  sees in the Visions but he has created a  way for Humanity not to be destroyed he  has created a way for Humanity to hide  now we all remember the scene in Dune  with the hunter Seeker device now  imagine a hunter Seeker device that so  finely tuned that not even a breath or  heartbeat can be hidden from it now  imagine that this device is also  self-replicating imagine that it reaches  a level of comprehension that resembles  prescience this is what leito foresaw a  machine that would seek out and hunt and  kill all humans until there were no more  humans this is the ixian problem this is  the Paradox of endless technological  innovation at some point eventually the  technology develops to a point where it  is beyond our control of it this ixian  dilemma is a mirror of the tleaksu  Dilemma the sleigh laksu are also  technological innovators On The Fringe  except they emphasize biological  technology their face dancer slave class  who they gradually improved again and  again throughout the eons eventually  grew far beyond their own control until  eventually they present themselves as  the god-like beings Daniel and Marty at  the end of the book Chapter House Dune  so when thinking about the ixian problem  and the talak suit problem it becomes  clear that at the heart of Doom has  always been this sort of warning about  the careless development of Technology  just for the sake of development it's  not saying don't innovate but it is  saying be mindful of where this could  potentially lead and it's also saying  that there need to be safe cards so that  like if it goes too far we can handle it  everybody wants a prescient  self-replicating Hunter Seeker device  until you can no longer control what it  is seeking out the thing about  technology is once it exists it can  never be put back in the box  think about nuclear weapons and how all  of humanity could be destroyed with just  the pressing of a few buttons once the  technology is created the cat is out of  the bag so to speak it is almost  impossible to stop technological  innovation humans seem to want to keep  improving upon things they build some of  you might have heard of the  technological singularity that's at the  core of this idea the technological  singularity is a hypothetical point in  time where technological growth will  become radically faster and  uncontrollable resulting in  unforeseeable changes to human  civilization the ixian problem is the  technological singularity the seeking  machines would be there the smell of  blood and entrails the cowering humans  in their Burrows aware only that they  could not Escape while all the time the  mechanical movement approached nearer  and nearer louder and louder everywhere  she searched it would be same No Escape  anywhere so Frank Herbert was concerned  about something that several authors  before him and an incredible amount of  authors after him were also concerned  about the technological singularity the  point in time where we lose control of  the technology that we are cultivating  and developing  if you look at the modern world and you  think of things like the YouTube  algorithm or Google the vast majority of  us have no idea how these things work  but there are also some programs which  are black boxes you put in input and it  gives you a result and no one  understands how it's getting the result  not even the programmers now of course  I'm not a computer scientist so I'm sure  it's a lot more complicated than that  but you can get my point essentially in  the Dune Saga Frank Herbert is making  the argument that we cannot stop  technological progress  but we can improve upon ourselves and  make it so that we are not so dependent  upon technology that our civilization  falls apart when it is not around and to  make sure we keep it in check so that it  does not get to a point where we cannot  control it and dial things back if they  get a little bit too intense if the AIS  start taking over the planet  alright thanks for watching guys what do  you think about these Concepts what are  some of your favorite science fiction  books that share similar Concepts let me  know in the comment section below just a  heads up for those of you that may be  interested my next graphic novel the LIE  behind the star is launching February  2023 you can sign up now to get on the  email mailing list to get notified as  soon as it launches more information on  my website link in the description thank  you guys so much  [Music]

